I shoot in a privately-owned but open-to-public indoor range that only allows
handguns. For rifles, etc. there is an undeveloped range on public land over
the hill near Palmdale. I've never had anyone get close to see what I was 
shooting there.  Once I went with co-workers to an area which they claimed
allowed shooting, but the sheriffs who helicoptered in were not amused. Due to
various factors such as the presence of beer, lots of scary looking guns, and
someones possession of pot (unknown to me), we should be doing time today.
Why we were let go is beyond me, I'm just ahelluva lot more careful now.

I don't know anything about the status of hunting.

                          - O Martin

