From: szabo@netcom.com (Nick Szabo)
Subject: Finished Selfish Gene; any comments?

I appreciated the game theory in _Selfish Gene_, but
I found even more valuable its fundamental insights into
human nature.  After studying this and other works of
the "sociobiology" school, human behavior, my own and other's,
becomes a much less mysterious and puzzling thing.  Individual+kin 
(gene) selection, reciprocal altruism, etc. have vastly expanded my 
capability to explain and predict a wide variety of human 
phenomonon in a wide variety of cultures.  Along these lines
I also highly recommend _The Evolution of Human Sexuality_ by
Donald Symons, which goes in-depth into the anthropological
literature from a wide variety of cultures, and delves into
the humanities, showing how a wide variety of human culture
relates to our "selfish gene" motivations.

> Am I the only one here taking the reading list seriously enough
> to spend money buying the books? 

I've bought SG, TMoF, and several others on the list.

